{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/432886-new-solar-sunday","id":432886,"title":"New Solar Sunday!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-08T12:09:36-07:00","id":432886,"title":"New Solar Sunday!","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>MELODIOUS ODE, the Wandering Minstrel</b></div> <br /> He was born and raised in a small threshold village where the very concept and sound of music were forbidden. Many times he had been whipped for idly humming tunes or beating out a rhythm on fences, but the boy seemed addle-minded and good for little else. He became an absent-minded young man without good prospects, regarded as something of a town idiot, until the stranger came calling. He was a traveling minstrel, a bard of many songs and stories, jangling with musical instruments. Quickly run out of town, the songful stranger sadly left, but not before inspiring the youth to lift his voice in true song for the first time.<br /> <br /> The villagers were horrified, and tried everything to shut him up, but they couldn't. Even at the town hearing, he joyously sang his defense, the shining mark on his forehead signaling a song so powerful that they could only stand and listen...to the ruin of all. For the injunction against music wasn't some idle whim of distant ancestors, but the only way they could ensure the perpetual sleep of the Behemoth called Song-Eater. While the visitor's music had stirred the creature, his sun-powered song finally woke it, and it came in its hunger. Most of the village was destroyed and its people slain, before he fled, drawing the monster after him, greedily devouring every improvising vocalization he could throw at it.<br /> <br /> He finally silenced himself long enough to lose it, and began his wanderings. He had many random encounters with many new and strange people and creatures, but the ones that made the most impression were those to do with his new passion for music. He eventually found himself in the Musician's Village, where he learned how to fashion many varieties of instrument; when he'd learned all they had to teach him, they gifted him with one of the true treasures of their home, the Unsurpassed Sanxian, bound with the musical soul of the village's founder. They sent him with a letter of recommendation to study the art of composition with one of their patrons, the Elemental Dragon Naresh, a connoisseur of music who bestowed upon him his current name.<br /> <br /> From Naresh, Melodious Ode learned the rules of creating music, from short, solo songs to hours-long symphonies for massive orchestras. The Solar flame within him burned brightly, and he churned out pages of music, relentlessly. But he still ached for others of equivalent skill to perform his works, and to play with and against. And he was still haunted by the spectre of the beast that he had unwittingly unleashed, who would gleefully swallow all the music in the world, until it finally drowned in mournful silence...<br /> <br /> Still, Ode has hope. He recently won a musical duel against a Faerie Prince, who informed him that the Song-Eater has a weakness, that which laid it low before: A song that even it can not swallow. He did not know this song himself, but hinted that it could be found in the realms beyond those of man, if only in fragments. Even now, he prepares to descend to the dead, whose dirges may recall part of the song he needs; and if he survives that, then must he dare the mad music of Malfeas, to play for the favor of the greater souls of the Yozis themselves. If only he weren't distracted by those recurring dreams of that Nightengale-woman who sings with a voice of silver...<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> Melodious Ode has a Mentor in Naresh, Arbiter of Northern Storms, and an Enemy in the Song-Eater. His Driving Passion is Learning and Performing all types of Music, and he has the Prodigy merit for Performance, which aids him in increasing his Specialties; he is quickly working his way up through the Charms the ability gives him. In addition to his Unsurpassed Sanxian, he also has an Ultimately Useful Tube, which he uses in its flute mode most of the time. He bears many other instruments, which he made himself with his Craft Specialty, but they are simply exceptional in nature, not magical.<br /> <br /> Most of Ode's development is in Awareness, Dodge, Survival, Integrity and Resistance. He prefers no to fight, but Naresh insisted on giving him some training in Melee (staff) for self-defence.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 07-12-2015, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T21:28:53-07:00","id":461853,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Freja, the Renegade Ancestor Cultist</b></div> <br /> Like most of the Barbarian tribespeople who call themselves the Tear-Eaters, Freja was perfectly comfortable growing up in and around Shadowlands, being raised to believe in her people's strength, and enjoying the bounty the tribe's raiders brought back from both the living and the dead. The one dark spot in her youth was seeing her beloved older brother return from his coming-of-age journey into the Underworld, one of the few who periodically fail and come back as a mindless zombie. Only once did Freja commit the greatest taboo amongst her people, by addressing him, one of the Nameless Dead, as her brother instead of the rotting slave he now was...<br /> <br /> Perhaps that was enough. When it was her turn to journey alone into the Underworld, to find the opulent encampment of the Great Dead and to offer her gift to her ancestor in hopes of receiving the right to bear his name among the Tear-Eaters, she too was rejected. Yet, when the wrathful Lich reached out towards her, it suddenly drew back in pain and terror, at the warm, golden light breaking forth from Freja's forehead. The girl herself was too dazzled by the deep, heroic voice in her head: &quot;Long have your people been deceived, used and abused by the dead. Light their way, and lead them forth away and out from this darkness!&quot;<br /> <br /> Taking back the enchanted ax her shaman uncle had helped her craft as a gift, Freja fought her way free from the Great Dead and their warriors, blazing with the righteous light of the sun. She ran, as fast and far as she could, until even the Essence powering her strides gave out. Rescued by a kindly village of ghosts, she pondered her next move. She could not go home again, for she had failed in the ways of her people. More importantly, Freja felt the truth of the voice within, and knew both the burden and the empowerment of the divine mission she had been given...<br /> <br /> Since then, Freja has extensively traveled the Northwest of Creation, her journey threading in and out of its many Shadowlands. Reviled as the greatest traitor to her people, she has fought off many of their raids, defending both the living and the dead against them. Always, she takes great pains not to permanently harm them, however, and tries to get them to see the truth of their enslavement to the Deathlord who dominates their lives and afterlives; dead Tear-Eaters are beyond help, as far as she's concerned, and she destroys them, and any other harmful dead, without hesitation or mercy. Her legend is growing, and has already reached the Crimson Fortress and its mistress, who smiles and plots to seduce the young Lawgiver into her service...<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> Freja is a young woman, still growing into adulthood, but with plenty of exercise rapidly strengthening her tall, athletic build. Her youth in a Shadowland has left its mark on her, leaving her looking somehow frail, despite her obvious fitness, and her unusually pale skin stands in sharp relief to her long, bright red hair. Like most of her hardy folk, she prides herself on not requiring much insulation from the elements, especially thanks to her Charms, and wears little save armor most of the time.<br /> <br /> Freja is a Zenith Caste Solar, whose Survival, Integrity, Athletics and Resistance aids her greatly in her wanderings through the wilderness of both Creation and the Underworld. She has grown famous for her use of her Anima power to both defend the living from the dead, and to save those she could not protect from rising to join the ranks of their killers. Her Presence Charms also greatly aid her in addressing both her enemies and possible allies, as well as invoking the Holy strength that empowers her. She has some knowledge of Occult, specializing in ghosts, which also aids her in combat against them.<br /> <br /> Freja's main combat ability is Melee, and she enjoys the Favored Weapon merit with her rune-scribed Grimcleaver of enchanted bone. In her travels, she has gained but one steady companion, a Steel Shadow she calls Dusk, as her Familiar. She has yet to succeed in destroying any of the Great Dead, but she has had multiple encounters with one of the very few to break free from the necromantic control of the Lover and to find his own path. This powerful Lich has offered to teach her more of the dead and their ways, and Freja is starting to believe that he may well be her greatest ally in her war against the Deathlord who has stolen her people...<br /> <br /> <i>(Yeah, I know it's a bit past Sunday now, but this PC was in my head all day at work, and I couldn't wait to post her here when I got home!)</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 07-12-2015, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T21:47:53-07:00","id":461868,"title":"","content":"I like it. A touch cliche, maybe, but a cliche done well, and with an interesting little twist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-29T22:24:41-07:00","id":461888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/432886-new-solar-sunday?p=461853#post461853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>(Yeah, I know it's a bit past Sunday now, but this PC was in my head all day at work, and I couldn't wait to post her here when I got home!)</i></div> </div> </div> </div>It's Sunday for another hour and a half here. You're fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T08:06:11-07:00","id":462257,"title":"","content":"No New Lunar Mo(o)nday? Lunar deprotagonist!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T08:14:51-07:00","id":462268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/432886-new-solar-sunday?p=462257#post462257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No New Lunar Mo(o)nday? Lunar deprotagonist!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/399276-happy-moonday-here-have-a-lunar\">There's a thread for that!</a><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T09:13:12-07:00","id":462341,"title":"","content":"Dammit! I knew I should have made a crack about Sidereals instead (e.g. Satur(n)day)!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T09:20:24-07:00","id":462345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/432886-new-solar-sunday?p=462341#post462341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dammit! I knew I should have made a crack about Sidereals instead (e.g. Satur(n)day)!</div> </div> </div> </div>You can come back tomorrow for Marsday :P<br /> <br /> Fun fact, french for Tuesday is Mardi, and Germanic for Tuesday is <i>T\u012bwesd\u00e6g</i>. Tiw is often equated to Mars.<br /> (Auxilliary fun fact: Mardi Gras literally means Fat Tuesday, which comes down to Fat Day of Mars... I wonder is Mars feels fat on Mardi Gras)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:lucida sans unicode\">Bearer of the legacy of Trauma Bear<br /> Need a dice-roller? Check out <a href=\"http://bit.ly/dicemat\" target=\"_blank\">Dicemat</a>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/43-fata-ku","name":"Fata-Ku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar43_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T10:07:29-07:00","id":462386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fata-Ku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/432886-new-solar-sunday?p=462345#post462345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fun fact, french for Tuesday is Mardi, and Germanic for Tuesday is <i>T\u012bwesd\u00e6g</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sunday and Mo(o)nday in the germanic languages are associated with the obvious deities as well. Friday is from Frig or Freya (both cognates of Venus). Wednesday (Woden, associated with Odin) and Thursday (associated with Thor) are further off.<br /> <br /> The romance languages (and Creation, by canon) take their cues from Latin:<br /> dies Solis, dies Lunae, dies Martis, dies Mercurii, dies Iovis, dies Veneris, dies Saturni<br /> <br /> And Latin in turn took them from Greek (I suspect many of the roots will be obvious):<br /> hemera Heliou, hemera Selenes, hemera Areos, hemera Hermou, hemera Dios, hemera Aphrodites, hemera Kronou<br /> <br /> Interestingly, the Indian days of the week are associated with the same planets, but the associations of the relevant gods, with the notable exception of Mars (Mangala), are very different.<br /> <br /> This concludes todays etymology interlude, now back to your regularly scheduled thread.<br /> (classics scholars, forgive me for butchering the accent marks, they are a pain...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 03-30-2015, 01:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T10:21:29-07:00","id":462395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/432886-new-solar-sunday?p=462341#post462341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dammit! I knew I should have made a crack about Sidereals instead (e.g. Satur(n)day)!</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/400943-sidereal-of-the-day\">It wouldn't have helped!</a><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T13:29:29-07:00","id":462633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/432886-new-solar-sunday?p=462386#post462386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sunday and Mo(o)nday in the germanic languages are associated with the obvious deities as well. Friday is from Frig or Freya (both cognates of Venus). Wednesday (Woden, associated with Odin) and Thursday (associated with Thor) are further off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you sure it's not Freyr?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/370-oriares","name":"Oriares","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar370_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T13:59:28-07:00","id":462654,"title":"","content":"Are you going to collect them yourself in a google doc or should one of the rest of us do it? ;-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Also, look at <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Ow3IPUb4QtgMb1y2evMSGlJxE2VmTEOvyhJDu2eMAAo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">the exalted fan collection</a> that we are making.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/80-truemonk","name":"TrueMonk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T14:22:58-07:00","id":462669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/432886-new-solar-sunday?p=462395#post462395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/400943-sidereal-of-the-day\">It wouldn't have helped!</a><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I CANNOT WIN QUITTING NOW","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T11:28:12-07:00","id":463669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oriares</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/432886-new-solar-sunday?p=462633#post462633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you sure it's not Freyr?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not an authority on the subject, but everything I can remember seeing has been consistent in associating it with Frig/Frigge/Freya. If Wikipedia is to be believed, in proto-germanic Freya's theonym was <i>frijaz</i> and Friday was <i>Frijj\u014dz.</i> Freyr/Frey, in proto-germanic, was called Ingwaz (Frey later added by the Norse from his title, &quot;Lord&quot;), so it seems unlikely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T17:50:28-07:00","id":464091,"title":"","content":"So is this a showcase? Or are others invited to make submissions? :3","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some Tunes for your Exalted Game? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1071249-exalted-tunes\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-exalted-tunes</a><br /> Want some help managing your PCs? <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882498-new-anathema-character-management-anathema-reincarnated\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...a-reincarnated</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2442-arian-dynas","name":"Arian Dynas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-05T11:20:40-07:00","id":469440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arian Dynas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/432886-new-solar-sunday?p=464091#post464091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So is this a showcase? Or are others invited to make submissions? :3</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sure, go ahead! Bonus props if you can base a Solar on today's particular Sunday...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TrueMonk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you going to collect them yourself in a google doc or should one of the rest of us do it? ;-)</div> </div> </div> </div>I really need to find a few hours to learn how all that works...sadly, I'm not as computer-literate as I really should be...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T20:51:32-07:00","id":588811,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>JAHN SUNSTRIDER, the Spacefaring-Adventurer</b></div> <br /> Jahn Krem had fought, killed, and bled for His Divine Lunar Presence's Thousanth Dynasty, and the people of the Central Empire, but in the end, all his conscience had earned him was a dishonorable discharge for refusing to carry out his orders during a routine &quot;pacification&quot; action. Disgusted with the Imperial legions, the ex-soldier defected to the Frontier, where he could at least live on his own terms. <br /> <br /> Since soldiering was all he knew and was good at, he made a living at it, aside from that short stint as a Sky-Taxi pilot. There was no shortage for hired guns, and he had a good enough reputation that high-placed organizations started asking for him by name. One such was an exploratory mission, that had obtained supposed maps and codes to Rael, the legendary lost planet of the Solars, at exorbitant price, and needed equally high-priced bodyguards. Despite misgivings, Jahn signed on...<br /> <br /> The mission went well, at first: The system was found, and the defensive perimeters let them in. Once they landed, however, it all went very bad. No code could save them from the engineered creatures, mechanicals and behemoths that had all been programmed to slay any non-Solar outsider, and Jahn could barely save himself, let alone those who had accompanied him. He was the last survivor, forced to watch helplessly as they all died, and set himself to go down fighting...when a golden miracle descended from the sky.<br /> <br /> The legends were true; at least one ancient Solar still lived here, and it was the famous Contentious Sword, no less! He had been watching, but had only been moved to act by Jahn's willingness to die fighting. Taking Jahn under his protection, he treated him as a lowly servant at first, but warmed up to him over the weeks and months, finally regaling the mercenary with long-unheard tales of the ancient days of the galaxy. Eventually, he started sparring with him, quickly training Jahn in the forms of superior swordplay long since forgotten. <br /> <br /> It was when he made Jahn demonstrate his mastery of the final striking technique of this style that the point of all this became plain. Contentious Sword dropped all his defenses, allowing Jahn to strike home deeply, and fatally. As he died, he passed his Exaltation to the stricken soldier, along with instructions as to what to do next, chief among them, not to waste his life and power as he had done.<br /> <br /> Jahn first proved his mettle by interring his masters' body in the golden tomb complex that he had long ago prepared for himself, which was a dangerous task in itself. Once past all the traps, a holo gave him two rewards. The first was a treasure of a lost age, which even Contentious Sword barely understood and none today could replicate: An Orichalcum Beamklave, one of the few to ever exist. <br /> <br /> The other waited hidden in an underground hanger: An Orichalcum Artifact starship, the <i>Invincible Sword Princess</i>, as sleek and beautiful as she was fast and deadly, and co-piloted by a spirit-program of the same name. Activating her eager engines and Anima Circuits, Jahn finally bade farewell to the only world he'd felt at home at, and ventured out into the canals between the stars to make a new name for himself...which would come to be &quot;Sunstrider&quot;. <br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> Jahn Sunstrider is a young Dawn-Caste Solar, who specializes in Melee, Firearms, and Pilot. He always carries his trusty old Starcaster as his primary weapon, but has several others to fall back on. Perhaps his most dangerous weapon is his Beamklave, which he has the Favored Weapon Merit for. As he learns to apply his Essence to the sword techniques he learned on Rael, he has been teaching himself the Charms for Single Point Shining Into The Void Style Martial Arts, of which he has learned up to the Form Charm.<br /> <br /> <i>Invincible Sword Princess</i> is a unique starship about the size of a space yacht, able to carry a crew of about 5-10, at most. Her Heavenly Guardian Defense shields make her tougher than her delicate build would suggest, and few ships are faster and more manueverable in direct combat. ISP herself often speaks as a disembodied voice, but can manifest as an image, either on the view screen or as a small figure on the controls. She recognizes Jahn as her master and will only take his orders, although she sometimes refers to him by her former masters' name by &quot;mistake&quot;, when she's peeved at him. <br /> <br /> As one of the first Solars in action in recent years, Jahn's more flamboyant activities have attracted the attention of various powers, seen and unseen, in the galaxy, many of which have begun to seek him out. Perhaps the most interested of these is the Seven-Devil-Killer, one of His Divine Lunar Presence's top assassins...and the bearer of the Moonsilver sibling to his Beamklave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T05:59:15-07:00","id":636914,"title":"","content":"I have started putting these and the other sample characters into a wiki placeholder that I am making <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Ow3IPUb4QtgMb1y2evMSGlJxE2VmTEOvyhJDu2eMAAo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> because there is so much good stuff being posted on the forum that I think I will forget where to find it if I do not. If anyone wants to join you are welcome :-) I guess it will allways be a work in progress, but maybe it is even more now than it will be later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Also, look at <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Ow3IPUb4QtgMb1y2evMSGlJxE2VmTEOvyhJDu2eMAAo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">the exalted fan collection</a> that we are making.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/80-truemonk","name":"TrueMonk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T21:03:25-07:00","id":663808,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>&quot;BAD&quot; PENNY</b></div> <br /> Penelope was born to a peasant family, but her dreaming heart led her to run away from the simple fisherman's life to join a passing troupe of wanderers at an early age. In their care, she learned the arts of dazzling and entertaining bored townspeople, and how to dissemble convincingly, skillfully inventing new pasts for herself to everyone she met. Penny learned how to avoid the Guardians of the Realm and how to bribe her way out of trouble when that was unavoidable. Most of all, she learned how to gain and exploit the trust of others...<br /> <br /> Penny realizes that it was one of her more daring schemes that led to a Magistrate and the Black Helms cracking down on her caravan of wanderers, and she's pretty sorry about that, but omelettes require broken eggs, and she'd learned about all she could from them, anyway, so it was time to move on. Besides, they really weren't doing much with all that money they'd gathered, when she could put it to much better use!<br /> <br /> So, Penny went to the larger cities of the Realm where she reinvented herself. During her wanderings, she had put her talent for observation and mimicry to good use, and in short order (and many new clothes and accessories), she found that she could pass herself off as a member of any strata of Realm society, from peasant to citizen to patrician. <br /> <br /> Swiftly making contacts in the Realm's underworld, Penny soon made a name for herself as a conwoman <i>extraordinaire</i>, dancing through society in a dizzying array of disguises, successfully grifting wealthy commoners and patricians who had more jade than common sense. Eventually, she overreached again, this time by fleecing House Ragara while in the guise of a minor patrician noblewoman from a Satrapy in desperate need of a loan. <br /> <br /> This broke one of the cardinal rules of the Realm's criminal element, who survive by staying under the Dynasts' radar. Drawing that kind of heat down on them will make them give up any sister criminal in an instant, and the Dragon-Blooded are quick to make an example of any that dare their wrath. <br /> <br /> What happened next depends on Penny's mood when telling her story: Sometimes, she claims to have been Chosen by the Unconquered Sun in the very act of pulling off her audacious scheme, which both necessitated her quick escape and enabled it, as well; other times, she tells of being exposed and captured, only her exaltation enabling her to escape her chains and prison right before her torture and execution. Or, she successfully slipped out of gaol on her own, and was chosen on board the ship taking her off the Isle, as though in reward for her resourcefulness.<br /> <br /> Whatever the truth, the newborn Solar took her act on the road.<br /> <br /> Penny traveled the Vermillion Road across the South, conning and grifting with increasing supernatural skill as she went: A sizable shipment of precious stones went missing from Gem, several nobles of the Lap lost their shirts in a pyramid scheme, many magistrates in Paragon lost their heads when the Perfect learned they had been swindled, the Tri-Khan won't reveal what he lost to her, but suffice to say, she can't show her face in Chiaroscuro ever again; Harborhead's economy almost crashed when flooded the market with fake jade, and her meddling in Varangia caused the permanent shut-down of many of its famous gambling parlors. As for An-Teng...she doesn't talk about what went down <i>there</i>. That place is just crawling with Bad Craziness...<br /> <br /> Deciding that the South had become too hot (<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />), Penelope set out for the East, eventually setting up shop in Nexus, a city after her own greedy heart! A place where, so long as you mind the Dogma and Civilities, no one can complain about you ripping them off because there <i>are no laws?</i> Hells, yes! Of course, nothing prevents your victims from taking their anger out on you, either, so you'd better be smarter, faster and sharper than they are, and avoid the notice of the Council of Entities and their Mercenary Companies...<br /> <br /> Penny maintains a few aliases in Nexus, including a wealthy socialite in Bastion, an eccentric artist in Cinnabar, a humble student in Sentinel's Hill, and a beggar in Nighthammer. She is greedily eyeing the Guild, having spent enough time studying its operations in her journeys across the Threshold to identify its patterns and weaknesses; successfully fleecing it would make her name across Creation, but it would also make her enemies as powerful as the Ragaras. It also galls her that she never got a shot at cracking either the impregnable Bank of the Scarlet Throne or the Vault of the Imperial Treasury; if such an opportunity feasibly arose, she'd find it hard to resist returning to the Blessed Isle...<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> Penelope has amassed a significant amount of experience in her adventures, much of which went into her Mental and Social traits (Specialties in High Society Disguise, Gaining Confidence and Talking Her Way Out of Trouble), as well as Backgrounds reflecting her Criminal Connections and Resources (easily 5; at this point, she's clearly in it for the thrill rather than the wealth). Her Merits include Silver Tongue, Jack of All Trades, and Cache; her Flaws are Vice (Stealing) and Wanted (House Ragara). <br /> <br /> Penny's Charm focus is on Stealth, Larceny, Presence, Performance, Socialize and Dodge. As of yet, she has no Familiars or Exalted Allies, although the Gold Faction is aware of her activities and is awaiting the right time to approach her. Her only Artifact is a set of Everyman Armor she stole in the South, but after an encounter with Shalrina in her shop, she is eager to earn one of the Goddess' Mask Artifacts (as well as her other services, if her enemies ever catch up to her...).<br /> <br /> PS: I can't decide on Penny's Caste: Is she a Social Night or a Larcenous Eclipse? Which would you make her?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T21:48:30-07:00","id":663870,"title":"","content":"Wow my own characters suck compared to these &gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> So many cool concepts!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T00:41:48-07:00","id":664036,"title":"","content":"I think it is too close, I would wait and see what rules represent her best.<br /> <br /> the lunars and sidereals are really good also. I gathered them in the link in my signature. If hand of omega does not do it, then I will give them stats when ex3 comes out :1)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Also, look at <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Ow3IPUb4QtgMb1y2evMSGlJxE2VmTEOvyhJDu2eMAAo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">the exalted fan collection</a> that we are making.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/80-truemonk","name":"TrueMonk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T08:07:50-07:00","id":664316,"title":"","content":"Thanks, glad you guys like, and can't wait to see what their CS look like!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T09:59:19-08:00","id":838697,"title":"","content":"Finally, new Solars for a new Edition! <div align=\"center\"><b>YUKI, THE SWORD-BRIDE</b><br /> </div> Not all of the sword-clans of Vaneha excel in swordsmanship, but the most prosperous still revolve around the sword in some way. This is true of the minor aristocratic Clan Kiji, whose hard-earned fame involves a secret formula they have perfected over generations, that allows their family to forge uniquely beautiful, as well as deadly, swords. <br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the fortunes of the family fell when they fell into the hands of the young Count Yuji, whose extravagance and out-of-control gambling threatened to empty their coffers and ruin their reputation. When he began covering his debts by selling off ancestral weapons, and even bargaining with the secret formula of the Clan, his little sister Yuki decided to act.<br /> <br /> Although competant with the sword as all of Vaneha's daughters are, Yuki was no great swordswoman, but she refused to stand by doing nothing; by law, only a blood-sibling could challenge the Head of the Family. However, she hedged her bets, in the likely chance that she would lose, by undergoing a ancient ritual wherein she symbolically married the Honor Sword of the Clan itself, ensuring that even if her brother cut her down, he would still ruin his standing in Vanehan society.<br /> <br /> Elaborately dressed, painted and coiffured, Yuki publicly challenged Yuji, and met with him as the sun arose on a dueling courtyard in Jibei. Furious, her insulted brother spared her no quarter, and as the resolute girl, who could barely defend against him, prepared herself to pass on to her next incarnation, she decided to at least give him a significant wound to remember her by. The bystanders gasped as her last-ditch effort surged with power and skill, guided by the hand of the rising sun itself, cutting the Count's sword-arm entirely off! <br /> <br /> Having suffered one of the worst injuries a Vanehan can bear, and faced with a blazing Anathema where his sister once stood, the Count had no choice but to surrender, and yield his status as Head of the Clan. Yuki, marvelling at quickly her swordmanship improved, spent the next week visiting the households who had gained her family's ancestral weapons and formula through the wasteful ways of her brother, challenging them for their return. Most saw no shame in capitulating, although some wished to test her steel, but all agreed to an Honor-Bond against using what they learned of her Clan's secrets.<br /> <br /> Yuki's true passion, however, had always been working the forge of her family, working and treating the molten metal in their unique way, and shaping some of the most eye-catching weapons the nation had yet seen. She had always dreamed of her name being added to the Honor Roll of the Kiji's most illustrious swordsmiths, and now, empowered by the sun's own industry, that dream was within her grasp. With a couple of weeks of practice, she found herself forging swords easily the match of any her family had ever made, and even expanding upon the formula to craft swords even more durable and sharp than any yet seen in Vaneha!<br /> <br /> But this would have to wait. Yuki was shortly visited by a delegation from the Sword Prince himself. In a polite, flowery manner, the ambassador hinted that, while Vaneha had no official policy regarding the Immaculate Order as no known citizen had yet become Anathema, it was perhaps best for all concerned if the young Lady of the Clan should delegate her duties and take an extended vacation, until such matters became clearer. Yuki agreed and set her affairs in order.<br /> <br /> In truth, this turn of events suits her quite well. While travelling distant lands has never been a dream of hers, Yuki is curious to learn how weapons are forged in other lands. And she has lately been plagued by recurring dreams of her last incarnation, a mighty Lawgiver sword smith who was the prize pupil of the fabled Sword Priest himself, and who created many legendary weapons that might yet endure in this fallen world, many in unworthy hands. Yuki, the Sword-Bride, has taken it upon herself to free these lost children, whether they be lost, buried or held in unworthy hands, and to restore them to righteous heroes who may use them to carve new legends, as well as to birth new wonders of her own, that this fallen, shadowy age may yet be redeemed and brightened through the shining steel of the sword.<br /> <br /> <b>Image: </b>Yuki is a young woman of average appearance, well-schooled in aristocratic dress, speaking and manners. Currently, she foregoes her formal wear, dressing in comfortable, but durable, traveller's clothes, never parted from the large sword-case that she carries her husband in, along with a small retinue of retainers. Few have seen her true aspect, a well-toned physique fashioned from many hours of handling the tools of the forge, complete with many scars and burns, marks of her trade that she takes great pride in. <br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> Yuki is a Dawn Caste Solar, with the anima banner of a phoenix and the Supernal Ability of Craft. She has Essence 1, with Craft 4 and Melee 3, but will soon raise all of those traits with all the practice she is getting. While she doesn't mind getting injured in the process of forging new swords, she is quickly learning the benefits of Resistance Charms, esp. as she favors taking blows over dodging them. She is also finding the application of her Essence to her studies of Linguistics and Socializing to be quite useful, and every swordfighter benefits from having a powerful Presence.<br /> Yuki specializes in crafting beautifully decorated Exceptional weapons, and is gaining enough experience through doing so to begin the next step of her journey, the crafting of magical blades. While her dreams are a guide, however, she still needs much mastery of ancient Occult Lore to be successful, to say nothing of access to exotic ingredients. <br /> <br /> Yuki's most treasured possession and companion is her &quot;husband&quot;, the Honor Sword of Clan Kiji. The most prestigious Vanehan families keep ancient Daiklaves in their sacred family shrines, the older and more storied, the better. Yuki's is a Black Jade and Moonsilver Daiklave named Kagehoshi, which, like all such swords, has long slept without a user to attune to it. Kagehoshi has finally awakened in Yuki's handling, and is somewhat bemused to find itself married, but plays its ancestral role well, and intends to hold Yuki to her vows. The constant practice the newlyweds have had has so far activated his most basic Evocations, which manipulate light and shadow. <br /> <br /> Yuki has the Merits: Artifact 2, Followers 1 (a small group who cooks and cleans for her, as well as carries her things), Influence 2 (Sword Clans of Vaneha), Language 1 (Riverspeak, necessary for arranging sales of supplies, materials and swords), Pain Tolerance (earned at the fires of the forge), and Resources 2 (befitting the head of a Clan, albeit a small one).<br /> <br /> <b>Intimacies</b><br /> Defining Principle: I make great weapons for great heroes.<br /> Defining Principle: I am responsible for the fortunes of my family.<br /> Major Tie: Kagehoshi (Respect)<br /> Major Tie: Clan Fiji (Loyalty)<br /> Minor Tie: Count Yuji (Disappointment)<br /> <br /> <b>Limit Trigger:</b> Seeing beautiful weapons being used for unjust ends.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T10:02:59-08:00","id":838699,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>XANTRA, THE DREAMING PROPHET</b></div> <br /> Deep in the Southern desert, notorious Dejaz is reknowned for its never-ending revelry, and visitors are always astounded at the flow of sumptous food, drugs, music and pleasure provided for the asking. But for a time, one wonder that the natives steered away from, was Xantha.<br /> <br /> One of innumerable children born from the ceaseless trysting in the city, and as carelessly abandoned, he was raised as all such are, trained to cater to visitors and to provide whatever entertainments they wished. However, his masters soon learned that none would touch the boy, as he was already clearly touched by some higher power that spoke through the child, and even the excesses of Dejaz could not tempt revelers to defile a holy child.<br /> <br /> Indeed, the Benefactors soon ascertained that the boy was blessed, or cursed, with a gift, of slipping into a dream-like trance at any moment, and pronouncing dire fates upon all nearby. The augeries were clear but not good; they dared not kill or silence the whelp, nor could they exile or bury him, lest some greater ill befall the city. And so, if they could not entomb him in some dungeon, they went in the opposite direction, and erected a tall, thin tower of stone, and placed the boy atop it, that he could prophesy to his hearts' content up where none could hear.<br /> <br /> But even they, the masters of the forbidden, underestimated people's desire to taste that which was forbidden. And so, even as they used mechanical contrivances to feed the growing youth, who sat still atop his stone tower around which the surge of merriment swarmed, there were those who climbed or swung near or arranged to talk to Xantha, seeking some news of their future. None went away disappointed, though few were gladdened.<br /> <br /> In those days, there dwelt in Dejaz a notable Raksha Lady, of exquisite form and motion, who sought to build her Story on the foundation that she could entice any, however holy and reserved, to lust after her. Behold, saith she, I shall dance my dance, and e'en yon holy child shall scamper down from his tower of purity to lie with me! And she began her dance, and all the city paused in its revelry to watch.<br /> <br /> It was said that her dance was so sensuous, that even those besotted with drug and drink were cured of their addictions instantly, for they only lusted after her thereafter; but the young man was moved not. The Fair Lady increased her efforts, actually deigning to strip off her luminous veils, which caused blind beggars to pleasure themselves to madness and animals to rut wildly in the streets, regardless of species, but still the boy was unmoved. Undettered, the Fae Madame, desperate at losing her legend, danced a spiraling dance up the side of the tower itself to reach the youth, for none could resist her once she laid her fingers upon them. But just beyond she laid her burning touch upon Xantha, his brow burst with a brightness more burning still, that cast the temptress down like a screaming meteor.<br /> <br /> Then did Xanthas finally speak to the entire city, in a sunborn voice that merely repeated words he was given: <i>Hive of Fools and Revelers! Thou iniquity has not gone unseen! Take thy sport while thou art still able, for the final hour draws nearer than thou knowest! Soon, these palaces shall fall upon thee and make for thine eternal tombs! Quit this place, and live! Or stay, and surely die.</i><br /> <br /> So saying, the newborn Lawgiver leapt from his tower to the outer boundary of the city, not setting one foot upon Dejaz's stones, for he knew that when he next did so, it would be either the Doom of the city or himself. As for the revelers of the city, lured and lulled by the Benefactors', they nervously laughed to themselves, dismissing his warnings as sun-madness, and rejoined their endless party.<br /> <br /> Xantha wandered aimlessly through the deep desert, finally coming upon one of the places where the world was weak, and tainted from the madness that lay beneath it. Here, the sands flowed as water, and Xantha swam through the rolling, cresting sand, until he came to a temple, the long-lost Floating Mosque, whose opalescent step he climbed to the doors. These were guarded by two great, glinting lions, a golden one from Heaven on the right, and a brazen one from Hell on the left, both of whom presented him with a riddle in two contradictory parts, the failure of which would entitle them to divide him as a feast between them.<br /> <br /> Fortunately for Xantha, his life had already given him the answer, and so the hungry lions were forced to bow and admit him. Within the Mosque, Xantha studied, and learned and grew in wisdom and power, and they say his tests and trials within were of a number only the Incarnae could count. Soon enough he departed, now able to speak but a word for the tempest-tossed sands to settle into a path as straight and solid as any in Creation, while ruby-eyed sandsharks with the voices of children sang hosannas as he strode forth back to the world.<br /> <br /> Now Xantha travels amongst the courts of the spirits and the fae, rescuing those luckless mortals who can be saved from their depredations, while reminding all of their proper place in the great chain of being, even if that means ruling over them for a time to set things right. He lets the Sun guide him across the South, ever aware that eventually, though not even he knows the hour, his steps will take him back to his birthplace for a final reckoning.<br /> <br /> <b>Image:</b> Xantha is an attractive young Southern man (although he has never noticed) and his constant walking across the burning wastes have given him a fit, though very lean, look. He allows his hair to grow wild, in accordance with the Southern custom that this designates one as holy. He pays little mind to his clothing, and when his inevitably wears away, he humbly accepts new clothes that townspeople gift him with, as he does gifts of food and drink.<br /> <br /> <b>Notes: </b>Xantha is a Zenith Caste Solar, whose Anima Banner is a golden four-armed statue sitting in a meditative pose. His Essence rating is 2, and his Supernal Ability is Integrity, with which he sometimes masters the powers of spirits while setting their courts aright. Resistance, Survival and Occult are his other major areas of focus, and he has learned Tiger Style martial arts from the gently harsh tutelege of his lion masters.<br /> <br /> Xantha has the Merits: Followers 2 (various mortals he has helped), Influence 3(Southern Spirit Courts), Language 1 (Old Realm), Manse 3 (Floating Mosque), Martial Artist, and Thaumaturgist (Inborn gift of prophesy, refunded upon Exaltation).<br /> <br /> <b>Intimacies</b><br /> Defining Principle: Mortals and Spirits must hew to their place in the order of things.<br /> Major Tie: Mortals (Protective)<br /> Major Tie: Spirits (Wary)<br /> Major Tie: Fair Folk (Antagonistic)<br /> Minor Tie: Lion Tutors (Respect)<br /> <br /> <b>Limit Trigger:</b> Being unable to help mortals suffering from supernatural abuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 08-29-2016, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T10:13:02-08:00","id":838704,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>ELDER GUAN, THE TRAVELING HEALER</b></div> <br /> <br /> Guan was born and raised in Wu-Jian, where, like many youths, he joined the gangs fighting for their turf to distinguish himself. Unlike many, he survived and settled down, graduating to the neighborhood associations who really ran Wu-Jian's communities, and who unofficially used the gangs as muscle. Guan married, had many children, and buried too many of them. These losses, along with the ones he had participated in on the rooftops of the city, motivated him to pour all his efforts into the poorly equipped clinic that serviced the people of his neighborhood.<br /> <br /> Guan turned the place around, inspiring the weary workers there, convincing those with wealth to channel more into better quality supplies and equipment, and even treating the sick and injured of rival neighborhoods, which strengthened relations in the long run. He also educated himself, becoming a self-taught physician of some skill, even teaching himself to read Old Realm so that he could make use of the ancient scrolls still within the clinic.<br /> <br /> The day finally came when Guan ventured below the populated layers of the city, in search of more ancient wisdom; there was little more he could do for his people, so either he came back with more to aid them with, or he vanished into urban legend, either outcome suiting him just fine. Instead, he came back with something else, due to a hazily-remembered encounter with an odd behemoth in the weirdly-warped shadowed alleys: Exaltation.<br /> <br /> From that day on, Guan's newly increased medical prowess became the stuff of legend, attracting even the wealthiest to risk coming to his little clinic for his aid. Soon, the place had more than enough money, and better still, the staff were trained to be as good healers as any hospital could boast. Guan decided to take his leave, to see the wonders of the wide world that he had only heard about before, to learn from the varied peoples, to bring his gift of healing to them and also to bring back what they had to teach on his visits back home.<br /> <br /> Earning room and board aboard the Denzik city-ship with free use of his skills, Guan soon earned a respected place within their hospice-barge. Whenever the small fleet of merchant ships disembarks from the Denzik craft to trade in various ports around the Inland Sea and in the Western Ocean, Guan went with them, drinking in the new languages, customs and games of people across Creation. Denzik traders spread tales of his acumen, and often came to drag him away to help some unfortunate with his skills.<br /> <br /> This led the Elder to encounter a wide variety of illnesses, both mundane and supernatural. Many of which were caused by curses of a wide variety, which has since driven him to increase his understanding of the supernatural world and its denizens. Guan has begun to broaden his reputation as a great medicine man into one as a puissant occultist and exorcist, as well.<br /> <br /> Elder Guan has yet to visit the Dreaming Sea area of Creation, which is well, as there is a domain there ruled by an exceptionally powerful spirit known only as The Maharani. What few outside of Heaven know is that this violet-skinned, six-armed woman is actually a creation of Guan's previous Solar incarnation, via his Occult mastery. She was his slave for centuries, serving him in all things with the hope of freedom constantly dangled before her. It took the Usurpation to actually free her, and she has traveled the world and grown very strong since, eventually settling to rule her own court of spirits and mortals according to her tastes.<br /> <br /> Now, the Maharani's Omen-Birds sing that her worst fear has come true, her former master has finally been reborn. She is uncertain if he can still establish any claim over her, especially as she has taken great pains to hide her true name from all in Creation. She ponders the wisdom of sending spirit spies to watch him, or even assassins to dispatch him, knowing that this will likely draw him to her that much sooner...<br /> <br /> <b>Image: </b>Guan is the very image of the wise old elder, a small, shrivelled Western man with a long, wispy beard and bushy eyebrows. He habitually wears dark, round glasses and smokes a long, clay pipe. He dresses in simple robes of particular shades of blue and violet, that his memories tell him physicians wore in the First Age to honor the Maidens of Serenity and Endings. Despite his obvious age, however, there is nothing frail about him, and he practically bursts with vitality and good cheer.<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> Elder Guan is a Twilight Caste Solar, with a Crane anima banner. His Essence is 3, and his Supernal Ability is Medicine. Occult is his second highest Ability. As a young man, he ran with the Wild Heron gang, and learned their variant of Crane Style martial arts; he has since learned to apply Essence to those teachings, and has taught himself most of its Charms, which he often uses to deliver Wound-Banishing Strikes in order to heal and set his allies' injuries in the midst of battle.<br /> His Merits include Backing 2 (Denzik Hospital), Language 2 (Old Realm, Riverspeak), Martial Artist, Resources 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Intimacies</b><br /> Defining Principle: I am the greatest physician!<br /> Major Principle: I will see all the lands and spread my healing there.<br /> Major Tie: Spirits that possess mortals (Anger)<br /> Major Tie: Wu-Jian Clinic (Pride)<br /> Major Tie: First Age Lore (Possessive)<br /> Minor Tie: Denzik (Gratitude)<br /> <br /> <b>Limit Trigger:</b> Losing patients.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 08-29-2016, 12:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T10:17:47-08:00","id":838708,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>THE RAITON KID</b><br /> </div> Born into the prison-city of Fortitude, the boy who would grow up to become the Raiton Kid was determined not to let the systematic abuse of being born with the stigma of criminality, the mandatory gang-initiations and wars, nor even the worship of the Prison-God, brand him for life. <br /> <br /> Upon reaching his teens, he embarked on the Rite-of-Passage every young person went through, the obligatory escape attempt. But rather than half-hearting it, being captured as expected, and accepting one's natural place in Fortitude, he seriously made an effort, researching the city's layout and guard patrols, and laid his plans well in advance, such as by bribing certain guard dogs with choice (stolen) meat. His efforts paid off, and, somewhere along the path to freedom, he Exalted.<br /> <br /> He's not actually sure *when*, however, which bothers him. Some part of him can't help but wonder if he could really have done it without the Unconquered Sun's empowerment. But usually he puts such worries out of his head, for he has other worries now.<br /> <br /> Adapting to life on the outside has been difficult, for he only had the stories he grew up with as his guide, and he soon learned that they were hilariously wrong. Soon enough (and definitely with the help of his new nature, which he accepts begrudingly), he picked up on how things work, especially among the criminal classes of society, which his upbringing has uniquely qualified him for. Still, the practices and beliefs of &quot;polite society&quot;, including honest, hard-working folk of all classes, frankly baffles him. He wants to understand them, and is a little worried that he fits in better with Guildsmen and the like. <br /> <br /> He earned the name &quot;Raiton Kid&quot; due to an incident in the Guild Border Town of Raiton's Teeth, where an innocent game of Boneyard escalated into a three-day riot wherein a prosperous caravan just happened to be fleeced of its many earnings. The Guild has put a huge bounty on the Kid's head, despite his protestations of innocence and coincidence. As if the bounty that fortitude put out on him, for being one of the very few to ever escape, wasn't enough...<br /> <br /> <b>Image:</b> The Raiton Kid is an average-looking Northern young man, although his rakish grin gives him a charm that makes him more attractive than he really is. He has gained enough money to dress in whatever style he wishes, and is still young and impulsive enough to want to show off, although he is learning the necessity of blending in. He is especially vulnerable to the wiles of beautiful people of either sex, as he had never seen anyone able to really make themselves so attractive in the dingy dungeons he grew up in. He is (slowly) learning that such folks can be as cut-throat as any other, although the appearance of true innocence and virtue gets to him every time...<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> The Raiton Kid is an Essence 2 Night Caste Solar Exalt, with a Raiton anima banner. Larceny is his Supernal Ability, and Dodge and Thrown are his main recourse in a fight, although he prefers to avoid such with Stealth. Survival charms help him to make it through the harsh weather of the North, evade tracking from those who would bring him in for a reward and empower his Familiar, an Omen Dog that escaped his home city with him that he calls Frostbite. Although not yet a supernatural martial artists, the Kid is quite skilled with fighting chains from his time in his neighborhood's Chain Gang, and is seeking out a Dire Chain.<br /> <br /> His Merits are Danger Sense, Familiar 2, Language 2 (Riverspeak, Guild Cant), and Quick Draw 1. He also has the Wanted Flaw.<br /> <br /> <b>Intimacies </b><br /> Defining Principle: I must make a huge legend of myself!<br /> Defining Principle: I will never go back to Fortitude!<br /> Major Tie: Beauty (Awe)<br /> Major Tie: The Guild (Comfort)<br /> Major Tie: Frostbite (Pal for life)<br /> Major Tie: Fortitude (Hate)<br /> Minor Tie: Chain Gang (Sadness)<br /> Minor Principle: Theft (Resigned)<br /> <br /> <b>Limit Trigger: </b>Being reminded of Fortitude.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-28T10:22:11-08:00","id":838709,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>CAPTAIN SUNSTORM</b></div> <br /> The boy who would grow up to become Capt. Sunstorm was born in the floating city of Gloam, a prosperous Realm port to the East, constantly surrounded by the sails of sea-craft, as testament to its popularity. With a natural head for figures, and a talent for smoothing over difficulties between peoples, the boy was groomed for a position with the Merchant Marine fleet, but it was the sheer act of sailing that made his soul soar. <br /> <br /> Until one day, when the ship he was on wandered too close to Threshold waters and was captured by pirates, who escaped pursuing Peleps pirate-hunters by fleeing up the rivers of the Scavenger Lands, where they were forbidden to follow. At the city of Nexus, perhaps the largest pirate port in the East, the ship and all aboard were sold to the Guild, who proceeded to dispense with the former Realm citizens as slaves as they wished. <br /> <br /> Fortunately, the boy was able to impress with his quick wits and agile words, and was retained by a Guildsman who had a need of a young mind to help him keep his accounts. The next ten years were a blur of disciplinary beatings, delirious rewards, lots of traveling and calculations, along with finding creative ways to help his master skim from the top. But however bad it got, and however much he missed his home and the sea, he was always well aware that there were others much worse off than himself; indeed, he often helped care for them in his masters' caravan before selling them to new masters, or worse still, the Fair Folk.<br /> <br /> Deliverance came when he was discovered using the same creativity he used to cook his master's books to arrange things so that some slaves were delivered to the wrong places, where they naturally escaped. Just as he was about to pay with his life, the Unconquered Sun set his mark upon the young man's brow, which stayed the Guildsmans' hand. Following Guild protocol for when a slave is Chosen, he promptly gave the newborn Solar his freedom, a generous amont of silver for his pains, and politely asked him to leave. The young man could have taken revenge right then and there, but he had learned patience...<br /> <br /> With the Sun enhancing his own gifts, expanding his seed money was trivial, and soon the boy was able to reinvent himself. Purchasing a ship and attracting a like-minded crew, he set out to become the River Province's most successful pirate hunter! It was a disaster. He'd underestimated how much of the Scavenger Lands' economy depended on piracy, few offered their help, and rivers constrained their mobility too much, unlike a wide open sea. <br /> <br /> While reevaluting his plans, he laid low at a Guild border station, where he knew how to blend in quite well. Everyone was marveling at a First Age wonder that a Merchant Prince had spent decades and considerable resources restoring: a ship that could said the very earth itself like water! With this miracle, he would have the most imposing caravans ever! Or he would, if he hadn't sold it to that non-descript young man for two dinar. <br /> <br /> Now with a ship that could treat the open land as his long-lost wide-open sea, the former pirate-hunter recreated himself yet again, this time as Capt. Sunstorm, scourge of the Guild and other slavers! Gathering his crew to him once more, they set sail, attacking caravans and border stations, raiding the Guild's coffers of slaves, silver and drugs, and freeing the lot (often destroying the latter), while still keeping enough coin to keep themselves well-off, of course. The Guild is not amused, of course, and spends increasing amounts to sic mercenaries and bounty hunters onto them, but so far, Sunstorm's speed, manueverability and First Age guns have given him the edge. <br /> <br /> Still, Sunstorm knows that his luck and skill can't last forever, and so he has negotiated safe haven with various spirit courts and even, ironically enough, Fae freeholds, for the inevitable time when it is time to hang up his colors for good and reinvent himself yet again. But for now, Captain Sunstorm sails proudly across the land of the River Province, raiding the wicked and freeing the helpless!<br /> <br /> <b>Image:</b> Captain Sunstorm presents himself as the very romantic ideal of the pirate that those who have never seen such might dream about, cultivating a rakish air while clad in colorful attire, weathered, yet still well-kept, always ready with a wink and a laugh. Only his chosen few in his crew see his true self, a haggered man, driven by nightmares of the miseries he contributed to, who longs to assuage the guilt that brings, and who knows that his very nature prevents him from returning to his long-lost family. <br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> Sunstorm is an Eclipse Caste Solar, with the anima banner of an Ox-Dragon breaking chains around itself with tosses of its mighty head. His Supernal Abiliy is Sail, with which he has enhanced both his ship and crew. Bureaucracy and Larceny also see a lot of use, as do Presence and Socialtize. Sunstorm is actually quite weak in fighting skills, never being able to find the time to shore those up. He prefers to Dematerialize when faced with real trouble, a trick he picked up from spirit acquaintances.<br /> Sunstorm's Artifact 4 represents his Land Ship, a large yacht that he has refitted as a pirate corsair, along with its built-in Lighting Ballista. He has rechristened this ship The Ox-Dragon, and crewed it with well trained Sea Devils (Followers 1), some of whom have learned Sea-Faring Hero Style martial arts. His First Mate is a mortal that he has enhanced with Underling Promoting Touch and Power Awarding Prana (Retainer 2). Their raidings have given him Resources 3, though sharing it with the crew and giving much to freed slaves reduces that to 2. Contacts 2 helps keep them ahead of bounty hunters hired by the Guild, which gives him the Flaw Wanted. Language 2 gives him Riverspeak and Guild Cant.<br /> <br /> <b>Intimacies</b><br /> Defining Principle: I will balance the accounts of my life, by freeing at least as many as I have exploited!<br /> Defining Tie: The Guild (Hate)<br /> Major Principle: I will escape myself by becoming someone better.<br /> Minor Tie: Ship and Crew (Pride)<br /> <br /> <b>Limit Trigger: </b>Failing to free someone.<br /> --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> There! Five new Solars for the Third Dawn! Not sure if they'd make a good Circle, but let me know what you think...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T12:44:45-08:00","id":843095,"title":"","content":"Man, over a hundred views all week, and only *1* like?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If these really sucked that badly, folks, I can't improve without comments!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T18:17:27-08:00","id":843223,"title":"","content":".... oh! I just thought I wouldn't mess with perfection. (Plus, I'm shit at using the like button)<br /> I'll give some feedback in the morning, m'kay?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T16:10:30-08:00","id":843658,"title":"","content":"<b>YUKI, THE SWORD-BRIDE</b><br /> This one may be a bit on the conservative side for Dawn Stereotypes. But, Vaneha is so well suited to the Caste, so how can you not.<br /> The story of her rise to glory is quite inventive on the other hand. Where did you come up with the Being Married to a Sword-idea?<br /> Kagehoshi is a pretty cool blade for a daiklave, especially with the antics they'll pull being married to each other.<br /> The intimacies are quite fitting, and I love the Trigger.<br /> <br /> <b>XANTRA, THE DREAMING PROPHET</b><br /> Right. Zenith-time. He's from Dajaz aka Sword &amp; Sorcery Vegas.<br /> What would we do without this place. The prose is <i>very </i>evocative of such a place, and I'll take notes on that.<br /> In fact, all of this is damn inventive, especially the Floating Mosque and the lions.A good template for a new player Zenith.<br /> A kung fu Jesus-esque wanderer with visions. I'm not totally sold on his appearance, as I think the robed strider with the wild hair have been done before.<br /> <br /> <b>ELDER GUAN, THE TRAVELING HEALER</b><br /> Ha. I like this guy. He's very much what I'd play for a Twilight, and he just oozes style.<br /> <br /> <b>THE RAITON KID</b><br /> Not at all what I expected from a Night Caste. A naive con-artist? That's pretty cool.<br /> Although, I find him to be the weakest from a narrative stand-point, but he's quite good for a pick-up game.<br /> <br /> <b>CAPTAIN SUNSTORM</b><br /> And *this* is why I love the Eclipse Caste. The versatility. And that name is gold.<br /> The tormented past is pretty good as well, although it could have worked with a bit more detail on his time as a slave.<br /> And the <i>Ox-Dragon</i>? Have you read Elric by any chance?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T16:11:23-08:00","id":843659,"title":"","content":"So. I made good on my promise. Hope you can use the comments for bettering yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T10:31:29-07:00","id":847179,"title":"","content":"First, let me apologize for the lateness of this response, and right after I asked for replies, too! All I can plead is RL, and losing internet connection briefly. But I'm back now, so on to business:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Growls</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/432886-new-solar-sunday?p=843658#post843658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>YUKI, THE SWORD-BRIDE</b><br /> This one may be a bit on the conservative side for Dawn Stereotypes. But, Vaneha is so well suited to the Caste, so how can you not.<br /> The story of her rise to glory is quite inventive on the other hand. Where did you come up with the Being Married to a Sword-idea?<br /> Kagehoshi is a pretty cool blade for a daiklave, especially with the antics they'll pull being married to each other.<br /> The intimacies are quite fitting, and I love the Trigger.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to push the boundaries of Caste, at least a little. Dawns revolve around martial conflict, but can one be, instead of a swordfighter, one who arms them? The fact that she specializes in weapons only is what separates her from a Twilight craftsman. I think the marriage came from thinking of the title &quot;the sword-bride&quot; as something a really good swordswoman might be called, and then (recalling the feelings of the sample sword in the core) just taking it literally!<br /> <br /> Also, I couldn't find a good place to mention it, but her dis-armed brother sinks deeper into drink and despair, until he is approached by a demon offering him a chance to regain his arm, his honor and even greater power than his sister, if he's willing to swear himself to the Yozis...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>XANTRA, THE DREAMING PROPHET</b><br /> Right. Zenith-time. He's from Dajaz aka Sword &amp; Sorcery Vegas.<br /> What would we do without this place. The prose is <i>very </i>evocative of such a place, and I'll take notes on that.<br /> In fact, all of this is damn inventive, especially the Floating Mosque and the lions.A good template for a new player Zenith.<br /> A kung fu Jesus-esque wanderer with visions. I'm not totally sold on his appearance, as I think the robed strider with the wild hair have been done before. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I felt the need to lay on the flavor pretty thick for this one! Xantha is also meant to be a look at the Integrity charms, which are probably THE single most improved Ability Charms in the entire set, with the possible exception of Occult. I like the image of him temporarily taking over spirit courts to set them back in order before moving on, claiming the powers of the top spirit to do so. That's also why he's a martial artist, to take advantage of the meditation charms; originally, he practiced Crane, but then I thought the lions might be more likely to know Tiger Style, so I switched it to that.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>ELDER GUAN, THE TRAVELING HEALER</b><br /> Ha. I like this guy. He's very much what I'd play for a Twilight, and he just oozes style. </div> </div> </div>As mentioned above, I really like how Occult is improved. I esp like that one can be an occultist who deals with spirits without actually having to be a sorcerer, and I wanted to see what that looked like. That's the main reason his Supernal is Occult and not Medicine. <br /> <br /> I forgot to mention it, but he has used his Twilight caste power to capture demons and elementals as his familiars. One of them is a Neomah, which he uses as a spy. Any ideas on what the others might be?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>THE RAITON KID</b><br /> Not at all what I expected from a Night Caste. A naive con-artist? That's pretty cool.<br /> Although, I find him to be the weakest from a narrative stand-point, but he's quite good for a pick-up game. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, he's probably the weakest, as I didn't have much of an idea for him, beyond where he came from. Judging from comments from Stephenls, I got his homeland wrong, but that's ok, as I had already come up with a &quot;prison city-state&quot;, that is basically what I based Fortitude on. If the actual canon Fortitude is that different, then I'll just relocate him to my place, Vor. <br /> <br /> The rest, I just made up as I was writing, even the name, which was likely inspired by a documentary I recently watched on Outlaws of the Old West.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>CAPTAIN SUNSTORM</b><br /> And *this* is why I love the Eclipse Caste. The versatility. And that name is gold.<br /> The tormented past is pretty good as well, although it could have worked with a bit more detail on his time as a slave.<br /> And the <i>Ox-Dragon</i>? Have you read Elric by any chance? </div> </div> </div>...A couple, but not much. Been meaning to get more into it. Is this similar to something in the stories? I've always liked Land Ships, and the idea of a Land Ship Pirate is actually one I'd visited before. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So. I made good on my promise. Hope you can use the comments for bettering yourself. </div> </div> </div>Yep, thanks for taking the time! I promise to respond to all comments in a timely manner from now on!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T04:12:09-07:00","id":847607,"title":"","content":"<b>Reg. Yuki's brother:</b> That's an amazing story-seed.<br /> <br /> <b>Reg. Demons:</b> Maybe a Perronelle? Or one of those Shadow-demons born from Mara? <br /> <br /> <b>Reg. the Ship: </b>In the Elric-books, there is &quot;<i>The Ship that Sails on Land and Sea</i>&quot; a pretty cool boat, built as a collaborative project between the Elemental Prince of Earth, Grome and his brother, the Elemental Prince of Water, Straasha, and now they're fighting over who owns the damn toy. The main character manages to get his hands on it in the first novel.<br /> I'm currently brewing on copying it for my own game, as a artifact ship forged by Pasiap and Daana'd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-15T09:48:22-07:00","id":847741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Growls</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/432886-new-solar-sunday?p=847607#post847607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Reg. Yuki's brother:</b> That's an amazing story-seed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Slayer would be the obvious caste, but maybe something else would be better?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Reg. Demons:</b> Maybe a Perronelle? Or one of those Shadow-demons born from Mara? </div> </div> </div>The shapeshifters? That's basically already covered by Neomah, who also have...other advantages. Stomach Bottle Beetle is a good choice, I think. Maybe a Thunderbird for muscle?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Reg. the Ship: </b>In the Elric-books, there is &quot;<i>The Ship that Sails on Land and Sea</i>&quot; a pretty cool boat, built as a collaborative project between the Elemental Prince of Earth, Grome and his brother, the Elemental Prince of Water, Straasha, and now they're fighting over who owns the damn toy. The main character manages to get his hands on it in the first novel.<br /> I'm currently brewing on copying it for my own game, as a artifact ship forged by Pasiap and Daana'd. </div> </div> </div>Hm, don't remember that, but it's been awhile! <br /> <br /> Land Ships are Artifact 3, but one that can sail both land and sea would be 5, definitely. Canonically, THE Elemental Dragons are even more detached from the setting than the Incarna, so it's pretty hard to imagine them making a tiny (to them) ship for any reason, and it would surely be Artifact N/A. Now, two Lesser Elemental Dragons, otoh, would work perfectly for this! But it's your story, so go with what feels right!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T19:43:59-07:00","id":849087,"title":"","content":"Ok, don't know how I missed this, but rereading the Land Ship writeup, it has a black *and* white jade strip along its hull, and is explicitly said to travel both land and sea! Huh, all this time, I thought it was restricted to land...and it's still Art 3! Combining it with a Folding Ship makes it Art 5, so keep that in mind...<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T10:26:39-07:00","id":885476,"title":"","content":"<i>In Honor of Mother's Day!</i> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>MITO, THE WANDERING LIONESS AND CUB</b></div> <br /> Mito's strident voice and inspiring charisma were so effective in raising resistance to the local Duke's oppressive policies (which took the life of her husband), even using her own home as a center to organize it, that the Unconquered Sun uplifted her into the Zenith Caste despite her late-term pregnancy. Her eventual delivery was thereby relatively quick and easy, and she carried her newborn babe close to her breast through the riotus streets, an iconic image that soon spread throughout the region as a symbol of heroic uprising.<br /> <br /> Her work done, Mito decided to follow her calling by the Sun by protecting the rights of others throughout the provinces, but saw no reason to give up her blessed status of motherhood to do so. Now she carries her child throughout the land, helping the people she comes across to right wrongs done to them in the Sun's name, while fending off those who would claim her and her child's lives, either to stop her protests or simply because of her Chosen nature. It remains to be seen how well she will do once the Wyld Hunt comes calling...<br /> <br /> Mito is a Zenith who excels in Performance (her Supernal Ability), especially Oratory, Presence and Socialize. She is quite good at Craft, which is good for making and mending clothes, and has constructed an innovative form of baby carriage, that appears normal, but is armored but quite lightweight. It can be quickly broken down in an instant, the carrying portion turned into a papoose, and the remaining parts becoming staves and wheel-based shields, which she wields expertly with Melee Charms. <br /> <br /> Mito's anima banner is a proudly waving flag whose pattern constantly changes; her Defining Intimacies are towards Freedom and Equality (Principle) and her child (Tie); her Limit Trigger is when her work requires her to neglect her child, however temporarily. <br /> <br /> <i>Happy Mother's Day!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T20:33:36-07:00","id":959644,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>MEGO, THE HOT-BLOODED SPORTSMAN</b></div> <br /> There is a confederation in the Threshold whose member nations spilled such massive amounts of blood in their history together, that they resolved to solve all future disputes amongst themselves as (relatively) bloodlessly as possible. They found their solution in a contact sport, where teams use strategy and martial skill to move a ball through zones on a field. Teams represent entire nations and political factions within each state, and the confederations' charter places strict sanctions on any member-states who fail to abide by the games' outcomes, however badly they may lose. This violent but honorable sport is called <i>Fistball.</i><br /> <br /> Mego was a legend among patrons, players and fanatical spectators. The Headman of his team, he rose quickly from his local league to the juniors, to the professional level, and was bidded and traded with lavish sums. While he wasn't the biggest, strongest or toughest player, nor the smartest strategist, his true strength lay in his enormous heart and driving passion, which inspired his fellow players to win, often against seemingly impossible odds.<br /> <br /> One such game, after Mego's team had battled back from the jaws of certain defeat, hinged on his daring a nearly impossible shot. As he let fly with the ball, he heard an unbelievably heroic voice in his head telling him to &quot;win one for the Sun!&quot;, and the ball flew with a precision and force clearly unnatural...Sadly, the game was called on account of Exaltation, and the referees conferred as to how to proceed.<br /> <br /> This had happened before, but rarely, and always with Terrestrial Exaltation. The rules were clear that said games must be suspended and replayed, and the formerly-mortal players moved into &quot;early retirement&quot;. Indeed, by this time, there were almost enough Outcaste players (or would-be players interested in the sport) to form their own league, if the Confederation weren't blocking those efforts! But none had ever exalted as a Celestial before, and although the member-states weren't Immaculate in faith, that propaganda reached far enough that they decided to play it safe and give Mego a more-than-generous severance package along with strong encouragement to seek his good fortune elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Quickly divesting himself of his earnings to those much needier than himself, Mego set out with the barest minimum of belongings, wandering the wilderness of the Threshold in search of a new purpose. He found it in helping people plagued by all sorts of problems, from common bandits to the strangeness of the Wyld. He had always been proud of serving as a symbol and icon of his nation, but now he realized that he could help people in a much more direct way.<br /> <br /> His latest adventure led him to a ruined castle-manse that all the villages nearby claimed held a terrifying apparition that regularly strode down the hill every full moon to lay waste to all he came across. Mego went there as the sun set, waiting for moon and ghost to appear. It did, wearing an elaborate golden and scarlet armor that it had possessed. Mego challenged it, exacting an oath from it that, if prevented from setting foot outside the manse throughout the night, it would give up its terrorizing ways; otherwise, he would willingly serve as its living vessel during the day.<br /> <br /> With its assent, the contest began; the two grappled and wrestled throughout the waning hours of the night, smashing what little was left of the long-dead manse's structure, the powerful ghost-armor driving Mego closer and closer to the gates...but, pouring sweat and gasping for air, knowing the people depended on him, Mego held firm. As the sun dawned, the armor straightened and opened its helm to reveal a face Mego had constantly seen in his dreams, thanking him before melting away in the purifying rays of the morn.<br /> <br /> Mego took the armor, his again with this cleansing, and donned it's eerily familiar weight. This encounter confirmed certain things for him: He now realized that what he'd been missing wasn't so much a purpose, as it was a team to share that purpose with. Inspiring others had always been when he'd felt most truly <i>alive</i>, after all! So now he sets out in search of others like himself...<br /> <br /> <b>Notes:</b> Mego is a Zenith, whose Anima Banner is a cheering crowd, and whose Supernal Ability is Resistence, reflecting his ability to absorb the worst punishment possible and <i>Never...Give...Up!!</i> Athletics, Brawl, Dodge and War are well-developed in him, from playing Fistball his entire life and improvising daring tactics to win, but he really shines in Presence. He has a Defining Principle of &quot;I always seize every opportunity to live life to the fullest!&quot;, a Major Principle of &quot;I always play fair and to win!&quot; and Minor Ties to Sports (Obsession) and Cheaters (Contempt).<br /> <br /> Mego's sole Artifact is the Corona Carapace, an Artifact 4 suit of Orichalcum and Red Jade armor. Interestingly, as he becomes increasingly attuned to its awakening essence, he perceives it as having the demeanor of a relentlessly driving coach, always pressuring him to go onward and upward, especially when it comes to awakening its Evocations.<br /> Interestingly, Mego own increasing prowess in Resistance has led to him manifesting his own spirit as armor, which he did for the first time at the climax of his duel with his previous incarnations' Po spirit...he's still unsure if he hallucinated this due to his extreme exhaustion, but in times to come he will refine this power still more. In time of his direst need, he will even learn how to enhance the Corona Carapace with his Glorious Solar Plate, wielding both sets of Evocations to devastating effect...<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">While reflecting on all the other N/PCs I've made and read about, it occurred to me that I'd never seen a Hot-Blooded Shounen Sports Star type before! This character owes more than a little to the main character of Akame Ga Kill (which is definitely NOT Akame!), and his evolving super-armor. The basic details came about while watching the Superbowl with my Dad, and maybe that would have been the best Sunday to post this, but I was otherwise busy. Hope you liked it!...Man, I really wanna make the rules for Fistball now...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":681,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","user":"Hand-of-Omega","date":". 10-17-2016, 02:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T13:33:56-07:00","id":960640,"title":"","content":"I love Yuki the Sword Bride, she seems very mythic. The only issue is that I'm pretty sure Dawns can't have supernal craft. <br /> <br /> Mego is wonderful too, I love the little mental image of the Unconqured Sun watching a fistball game on a screen in the Jade Please Dome and cheering Mego on so much that he accidentally exaalts the athlete. <br /> <br /> Those are the ones that really capture my imagination. I think that come sunday I'll post one of my solars. Lord knows I have too many.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T09:23:52-07:00","id":967359,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\">JUBILANT HARP</div> <br /> Jubilant Harp grew up in one of the many petty kingdoms of the River Province. He showed an early talent for music, but his family would have preferred he focus on his chores. When a traveling show came to his village he ran away to it and earned his keep as a musician for the show. He threw himself into music with a passion and dedication that would have greatly surprised his parents.<br /> <br /> When he was grown to adulthood the traveling show came to a principality whose interpretation of the Immaculate Philosophy banned excesses such as music. While the traveling show moved through the principality quietly, Jubilant Harp stayed, unable to countenance a place that actually banned music. Finding some like minded youths, he trained them in music and went to the princess to argue his case. Their performance so moved the princess that she immediately lifted the ban on music.<br /> <br /> Emboldened by this success, Harp and his band made a living as traveling musicians, as he had inherited a wanderlust from the show he had joined as a youth. He played in the worst dives, and the grandest palaces. He participated in his share of bar brawls, and became addicted to LSD when he heard of it's purported creativity enhancing properties. His reputation and his fortunes grew, and soon he was giving command performances wherever he went. He has given concerts for the gods of Great Forks and for the General Staff of Lookshy, he even played for the Scarlet Empress herself a year before she disappeared. Through it all he never stopped playing for the poor and destitute, believing strongly that music was for everyone.<br /> <br /> His legend grew to reach even into hell itself. One day a few years after Empress had disappeared, his band was approached with an offer to give a command performance for the Yozi Malfeas, the King of Hell. He discussed it with his band, and eventually they decided to agree. They made the five day trek across the Endless Desert, and gave a concert to the Brass Dancer with all His souls in attendance.<br /> <br /> In the middle of this concert time seemed to slow, and a golden figure with for arms appeared before him, charging him with using his music to inspire the world to greatness. Then the figure looked at the Brass Dancer, and advised Jubilant Harp to play like his life depended on it, because it really really did.<br /> <br /> Pouring everything he had into the concert, Malfeas rose to dance, so pleased was He with the performance. Jubilant Harp gave an Encore at Malfeas' demand, then attempted to get gone before the Ruler of Hell remembered why he hated Solars. Yet Ligier had other plans, and intercepted the band before they could finish packing their essentials. He complimented Harp and his band, saying that Malfeas and all His Souls were well pleased with the performance, and that he would like to forge a proper instrument for Harp.<br /> <br /> Not really able to say no, Harp and his band stayed a little longer, and Ligier took Harp under his wing, making for him not just an Artifact Guitar, but also arms and armor fit for one of Harp's new status. He also taught Harp sorcery. Ligier's aim was to secure the young Solar as an ally, and in this he succeeded, Harp feels strongly indebted to the Fetich Soul of Malfeas.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, after Ligier had finished forging Jubilant Harp's Panoply and he had learned of the Musical styles current in Hell, Harp ventured back into creation to fulfill the task given to him by the Unconquered Sun, to inspire the world to greatness with his music.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Notes</b>: Jubilant Harp is a Zenith with supernal Performance, his anima banner is rocknroll concert pyrotechnics. He has the Infernal Nobility merit for Liger's sponsorship of him, and his control spell is Invulnerable Skin of Bronze. He has 3 artifacts, a 4-dot Guitar, a 3-dot Chain Shirt, and a 3-dot set of Razor Claws. He has extensive contacts among musicians (3 dots), and speaks Old and High Realm in addition to his native Riverspeak. He has resources 2 as a phenomenally successful musician, and his 1 dot of followers represents his band. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T10:59:35-07:00","id":972018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/432886-new-solar-sunday?p=960640#post960640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love Yuki the Sword Bride, she seems very mythic. The only issue is that I'm pretty sure Dawns can't have supernal craft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I somehow missed how the Supernal rules worked back then. Still, that's something I'd be willing to houserule for the sake of a cool character concept. Or maybe she'd work better as a Twilight favoring Melee?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mego is wonderful too, I love the little mental image of the Unconqured Sun watching a fistball game on a screen in the Jade Please Dome and cheering Mego on so much that he accidentally exaalts the athlete. </div> </div> </div>Hehe, and then he has too sheepishly claim &quot;I <i>meant</i> to do that&quot; to a smirking Luna!<br /> <br /> Those are the ones that really capture my imagination. I think that come sunday I'll post one of my solars. Lord knows I have too many.[/QUOTE]<br /> Jubilant Harp is pretty cool (Solar Jimi Hendrix?)! But...when exactly did he exalt? It's pretty unlikely that Lookshy's General Staff would request such a performance, although I could see Malfeas doing so. Also, while you can certainly have LSD existing in Creation, I think Rasp Spider Venom might make a better drug of choice for him...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T11:29:02-07:00","id":972031,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><i><b>???</b></i><br /> </div> The first thing he remembers is waking up on a beach, the surf washing over him, as he gripped a stick-like object imbedded into the ground as if for dear life itself. Pulling himself up, he saw the blood from his injuries all over his tattered clothes, and bodies sprawled among the remains of a shipwreck...and he quickly realized that he could recall nothing else, not even his own name and identity. Searching the bodies provided no clues, only articles of better clothing and some money, and so he set forth, wandering aimlessly until he came to a town, by which time his wounds had mostly healed almost miraculously.<br /> <br /> This town had been ruled by a single gang until the recent demise of its leader, after which his two lieutenants each attempted to seize control, splitting the mob in two and terrorizing the relatively-peaceful township with escalating violence in its streets. Seeking a much-needed drink, he quickly found himself in an altercation some young punks, and surprised no one as much as himself with how easily he took them out. Red Harvest, one of the new bosses, offered him a job as an enforcer, which he accepted after scoping out the situation. <br /> <br /> The next week was a masterstroke of intrigue, as he instinctively manipulated events, subtly egging both groups on to their eventual destruction, mostly without having to lift a finger himself. When the final showdown came, he was again astonished at the surging energy that leapt to his fists and kicks at his command, as much as it had come to his tongue and suggestions earlier. By week's end, the bandits were finished, the people could rebuild a truly peaceful home under their own rule, and he had to move on. <br /> <br /> Since then, he has wandered aimlessly, hoping to come across some hint as to who and what he really is, or someone who will recognize his face. He has worked for the Guild, traveling far as a guard on their caravans, but has so far discovered nothing familiar and no one who knows him, although some of the gods and ghosts he has encountered and occasionally fought with have hinted that they at least know *what* he is, but they are maddeningly vague about it. And so he continues his journey for enlightenment about himself...<br /> <br /> <i><b>Notes:</b></i> Along with his name, his caste and even anima banner are completely unknown (Dawn or Night are likely, but Zenith and Eclipse could also fit the pattern described above); he unconsciously channels Essence from his Personal Pool, and uses mostly Excellencies and similarly subtle magic, and so doesn't often come across as supernatural. It's even possible that he may not even be a Solar at all, but an Infernal or Abyssal under some sort of magic that makes him seem like a Solar! <br /> <br /> The &quot;stick&quot; alluded to above is actually the hilt of his daiklave, which he stabbed into the ground as his last act before passing out. If he makes his way back there and pulls it out (it will resist anyone other then him), then he may start regaining flashes of memory...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T11:35:55-07:00","id":972036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/432886-new-solar-sunday?p=972031#post972031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This town had been ruled by a single gang until the recent demise of its leader, after which his two lieutenants each attempted to seize control, splitting the mob in two and terrorizing the relatively-peaceful township with escalating violence in its streets.</div> </div> </div> </div> Wait, is this-<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Red Harvest </div> </div> </div> So it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T21:26:36-07:00","id":972340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/432886-new-solar-sunday?p=972018#post972018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jubilant Harp is pretty cool (Solar Jimi Hendrix?)! But...when exactly did he exalt? It's pretty unlikely that Lookshy's General Staff would request such a performance, although I could see Malfeas doing so. Also, while you can certainly have LSD existing in Creation, I think Rasp Spider Venom might make a better drug of choice for him...</div> </div> </div> </div>He exalted during his performance for malfeas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T23:26:22-07:00","id":988709,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>KALVALA</b></div> <br /> The most fortunate of those born in mystic Ysyr are those with an active talent for sorcery, which guarantees them entry into its ruling class. But of those born into the rest of its society, perhaps the most fortunate are those whose Essence-created mutations give them a chance at a better life. Such was arguably the fate of Kalvala, an already pretty girl, whose feline appearance only added to her exotic appeal...at least, so claimed her parents, when they sold her to the Child-Hawkers.<br /> <br /> The girl Kalvala persued her lessons with feverish abandon, allowing her tutors to shape her into the perfect pleasure slave, especially skilled at dance, story-telling, and pain-relieving massage. And so she caught the eye and coin of Sorcerer Umir, who brought her to his Tower Surreal. As masters went, he was decent enough, not punishing her mistakes harshly, waiting till she was of age to take her into his bed, and not asking anything too demanding of her therein. <br /> <br /> In addition to her usual activities, Kalvala also entertained her master with her comedic antics; she was so good at this, that Umir began to bring her along to his meetings with other sorcerers, ostensibly to show off her beauty, but really so that she could afterwards regale him with exaggerated impressions of them. Little did Umir guess that she also performed the same function for the other slaves of his household, with himself as the subject matter!<br /> <br /> To complete these mockeries, Kalvala even learned some of the terminology she'd overheard from her master and his fellows. In his amusement, Urim even broke the law of his land, by teaching her the secret cant of the rulers, so that she could better ape his rivals. Noticing her facility with these terms, he didn't stop there, and before she knew it, Kalvala had learned enough about the materials and functions of his sacred sanctum to assist her master during his rituals.<br /> <br /> Finally, the hubris of Urim overreached his wisdom, and he called up that which he could not put down. Incensed by his temerity, the statuesque demoness danced through the air and performed a salterello over him that twisted his body and bones into a bloody puzzle. The horrified Kalvala knew that flight was pointless, and that her meager occult knowledge could not save her ersatz family from suffering the demon's wrath, and so she fell back on the only skill she possessed that might.<br /> <br /> Recognizing even in the demon's most casual movements that of a master dancer, she moved before her with a sultry gait, and let her body deliver an unspoken challenge. Whether from ancient nightmare or mortal slave, the language of dance was universal, and the demon, anger lessened by amusement, took up the challenge. Into the night the two danced at each other, even though the outcome was never truly in doubt. As her breath grew short and her limbs heavy, Kalvala knew all was lost, but pinned all her hopes on one thrilling acrobatic display. As she landed in a dramatic pose, all were astouded by the golden light that burst forth from her, as was she by the empowering, encouraging voice within that told her: &quot;You've GOT this, Kalvala. Now let's show this infernal bitch how we do things in Creation!&quot;<br /> <br /> Her opponent sized her up with shock and delight, seeing a truly worthy challenge suddenly appearing before her: it was ON.<br /> <br /> Neither dancer held anything back, their movements, improvisations and combinations dazzling the slaves who fearfully watched, and who would never be able to express the wonder blazed into their brains for the rest of their lives. By the time the sun peeked over the horizon, both dancers came to a halt. Kalvala was drenched in sweat, her pounding feet bleeding all over the floor; a newborn Solar is an impressive thing, but even they have their limits, and both knew without speaking who had won the contest.<br /> <br /> Still, the demon found herself impressed and fascinated. She finally spoke, offering the young Lawgiver a choice to grow with her help. Seeing little option, and curious despite herself, Kalvala agreed, and drew close for one last dance, an intimate tango that left her spinning alone. As she recouperated that day, she conferred with the chief steward of the household, who explained that once the other overlords of Ysyr learned of their master's death, they would weep openly, while proceeding to divine all of his belongings amongst themselves, including the slaves. <br /> <br /> Not wishing to lose her family, and unsure of her status in Ys society due to her new condition, Kalvala hit upon a solution: Umir was one of those few eccentric sorcerers who had revived an out-of-date custom of always wearing heavy robes, guantlets and masks in public, to hide his physical perfection from unworthy eyes. If she wore his vestments, she could perfect her already-good impersonation of her former master, and keep the household together, at least until they could figure else something out...<br /> <br /> That was a year ago. Kalvala has perfected her imposture of her master, whose increased reclusiveness isn't all that unusual for a master sorcerer of Ysyr. The slaves of the Tower Surreal have all accepted her as their new mistress, although she asks little of them beyond maintaining the place and keeping their shared secret. Most of her days and nights she spends in her sacred sanctum, honing her increased skills of both magic and dance. <br /> <br /> She has no wish to keep up this deception forever. Indeed, Kalvala has come to realize that, in time, she can grow far more powerful than any sorcerer of Ysyr. She plans to wait until she attains this greater power, then publicly reveal her true identity and turn Ysyrian society on its head, as a mutant slave takes the long-vacant but undeniable position of Archmage...<br /> <br /> Notes: Kalvala is a Solar of the Zenith Caste, whose Anima Banner is a group of scintillating backup dancers. Her Supernal Ability is Performance, and she has developed most of the Dancing and Voice Charms (she hasn't had much time or opportunity to learn the Sex Charms, but she is likely to be quite good at them!); she also has a good grasp of Presence, and Larceny helps her to flawlessly impersonate Urim. Occult is her most developed Favored Ability, giving her access to Terrestrial Circle Sorcery. <br /> <br /> Kalvala's Control Spell is Stormwind Rider, and she has a Shaping Ritual that gives her sorcerous motes through dancing. Her pact with Stanewald gives her the Infernal Nobility Merit, and she hones her skills through dancing with a Gilmyne named Sattriya, who brings her gifts and advice from Stanewald each time she is summoned. Her impersonation of Urim has given her the Merits of Manse 3, (Tower Surreal), Resources 2, Influence 2 (Ysyr ruling class), Followers 1 (slaves of the Tower Surreal), as well as his sorcerous infrastructure, including many exotic components; her personal Merits include Mentor 2 (Stanewald), Unusual Hide (Fur), Tail and Cat Ears.<br /> <br /> Her most developed combat ability is Dodge, which she supplements with Battle-Dancer Method. Despite the urgings of her bodyguard, Kalvala shows little interest in learning the arts of self-defense; after all, what are bodyguards for? However, she has recently come across something in her readings which has gained her interest, something called the Dreaming Pearl Courtesan...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-21T12:45:34-07:00","id":991069,"title":"","content":"Are we allowed to use our own headcannons for say...cities or areas of creation for the sake of these? Because I've got one I think is pretty good, but it pretty much overhauls Randan entirely from what it was in 2nd ed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12184-lazzerusthanatos","name":"LazzerusThanatos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12184_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T08:12:12-07:00","id":996078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LazzerusThanatos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/432886-new-solar-sunday?p=991069#post991069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we allowed to use our own headcannons for say...cities or areas of creation for the sake of these? Because I've got one I think is pretty good, but it pretty much overhauls Randan entirely from what it was in 2nd ed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hesh yeah! If you want to post your idea for your Solar Dolphin character for your &quot;Exalted Under the Sea&quot; campaign, then go for it, no canon-police here!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-31T18:18:38-07:00","id":996373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/432886-new-solar-sunday?p=885476#post885476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>In Honor of Mother's Day!</i> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>MITO, THE WANDERING LIONESS AND CUB</b></div></div> </div> </div> </div>This one is actually quite near one of my players' concepts. Her exaltation concept was that, while in labor, her village was attacked. Just as she was doing the final push she sees her husband cut down at the threshold of their house. Her overriding thoughts was that she will not let her child die or grow up in a world where such things could happen. She exalted at that point and grabbing her child, still attacked to her by the umbilical cord, struck down her husband's killer and then proceeded to rally the other villagers. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}